## Edge cases

- `scripts/test-design-structure.sh` pins the exact two-line settle dispatch directive. Keep those two lines adjacent.
- Markdown compression can accidentally change behavior by deleting repeated guardrails. Keep load-bearing duplication where it prevents misrouting or stale state.
- Rewording operator-visible `⏩` breadcrumb strings saves tokens but changes live `/design` output; those four lines stay verbatim even though `make test-design-structure` does not pin them.
- Blank-line-only reductions do not count as useful ratchet headroom. The acceptance needs real content-token reduction.
- The baseline writer regenerates both gated skills. Verify that `/implement` metrics do not change unexpectedly.

## Failure modes

- If `lint skill-closure-growth --write` increases any metric, revert the baseline update and compress the Markdown further.
- If Markdown shrinks but baseline regen is skipped or not committed, `python3 python/cli.py lint skill-closure-growth --skill design` still passes (one-directional growth only); CI fails on `test_committed_baseline_matches_fresh_scan` in `python/tests/lint/test_lint_skill_closure_growth.py`.
- If `make test-design-structure` fails, restore the exact pinned literals it names.
- If markdownlint fails, fix formatting without expanding prose unless needed.
- If the 15% reduction is not reached, make a second pass on duplicated setup, behavior, and output wording before touching any behavior-bearing text.

